<title>USA: Georgia Power Ga. nuke at 23 pct power - NRC.</title>
<headline>Georgia Power Ga. nuke at 23 pct power - NRC.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-10-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Georgia Power Co's 1,162 megawatt (MW) Vogtle 2 nuclear power unit, which was manually shut late Monday, has restarted and is at 23 percent power, the Nuclear Regulatory Commission said Wednesday.</p>
<p>The company earlier said the unit located in Waynesboro, Ga., was shut due to a malfunctioning feedwater regulator valve.</p>
<p>At 0916 EDT, a company spokeswoman said the unit had reached 35 percent power and should resume full power by week's end.</p>
<p>Georgia Power's other Vogtle unit, with an identical generating capacity, is operating at full power.</p>
<p>Georgia Power is a unit of Southern Co.</p>
<p>-- New York Power Desk +212-859-1628</p>
